    "Ledger ID": "Balance is a projection over this ledger, not a stored column. Comp-off expiry, joiner proration and the early-return reversal all fall out of the ledger model — LL-0022 and LL-0023 are two credits for the same person on two separate 60-day clocks, which a single balance cannot express. ADDED v1.1: LL-0031 to LL-0035 give the January rung of the proration ladder and a second worked example of the six-month catch-up — E1069 already past it, E1067 landing on 16 September during the demo window. RECONCILED v1.1. Sheet 19 held six comp-off credits; the ledger carried only three of them and none of the consumptions or the lapse, so a balance built from the ledger disagreed with the comp-off register for four of the five workers. Every credit, availing and lapse in sheet 19 now has a matching ledger movement, and 53_Leave_Balance_AsOn is derived from this sheet alone. Reconcile the two before the demo — being asked to explain a balance and finding the ledger short is the worst moment to discover it.",
